# Open-weights model for the agent of the lab (lab agent: OpenCode with scripts/opencode-open.jsonc) and, with
# LLM_BACKEND=open, for step 5 (lab suggest). Both also run on Claude Code: AGENT_BACKEND=claude, LLM_BACKEND=claude.
# Copy this file to .env.llm (not versioned) and replace the REPLACE_ME values.
# OPEN_BASE_URL ends with /v1: protocol openai calls <base>/chat/completions, protocol anthropic <base>/messages.
# OpenCode needs tool calls and the real window. On vLLM:
#   --enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser <parser of the model, e.g. qwen3_coder, hermes, openai for gpt-oss>
#   --max-model-len <OPEN_CONTEXT>

# Profile A (default): Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (125B MoE, 6B active) on a vast.ai instance, image vllm/vllm-openai:nightly
# (vLLM >= 0.30). The FP8 checkpoint has 173 GiB: 8x H100 80GB as in https://recipes.vllm.ai/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next,
# host RAM >= 64 GB for its 51B N-gram table offloaded to the CPU. The port is public, hence --api-key:
#   vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8 --served-model-name qwen-flash-125b --api-key <key> --max-model-len 262144 \
#     --tensor-parallel-size 8 --enable-expert-parallel --moe-backend triton \
#     --enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser qwen3_coder --reasoning-parser qwen3
# In OPEN_BASE_URL, REPLACE_ME is <public IP>:<external port of 8000> (IP/ports on the instance card).
# OPEN_MODEL is the --served-model-name, OPEN_CONTEXT the --max-model-len. The model thinks before it answers:
# OPEN_MAX_OUTPUT leaves room for the thinking and the answer.
OPEN_PROTOCOL=openai
OPEN_BASE_URL=http://81.183.231.113:14734/v1
OPEN_API_KEY=eb34a77d548fd5e6510f8b1081d4e78088bf5a47a712df0118d91d06f1032605
OPEN_MODEL=qwen3.6:35b-a3b-coding
OPEN_CONTEXT=262144
OPEN_MAX_OUTPUT=32768

# Profile B: vast.ai Serverless endpoint behind the OpenAI proxy of vast.ai. The key is the vast.ai API key
# (Account page), the model is set by MODEL_NAME on the endpoint and the proxy ignores OPEN_MODEL.
# OPEN_PROTOCOL=openai
# OPEN_BASE_URL=https://openai.vast.ai/REPLACE_ME/v1
# OPEN_API_KEY=REPLACE_ME
# OPEN_MODEL=served-model
# OPEN_CONTEXT=REPLACE_ME

# Profile C: local Ollama. Start the server with: OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=65536 ollama serve
# OPEN_PROTOCOL=openai
# OPEN_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# OPEN_API_KEY=ollama
# OPEN_MODEL=gpt-oss:20b
# OPEN_CONTEXT=65536

# Profile D: endpoint with the Anthropic Messages API, e.g. Ollama Cloud (key: https://ollama.com/settings/keys,
# model list: curl https://ollama.com/api/tags) or the hackathon endpoint.
# OPEN_PROTOCOL=anthropic
# OPEN_BASE_URL=https://ollama.com/v1
# OPEN_API_KEY=REPLACE_ME
# OPEN_MODEL=REPLACE_ME
# OPEN_CONTEXT=131072

# Backends: the agent defaults to OpenCode on this endpoint, step 5 to Claude Code (lab serve offers both).
# AGENT_BACKEND=opencode
# LLM_BACKEND=claude

# Step 5 (lab suggest) with LLM_BACKEND=open uses the same endpoint, key and model unless these are set:
# LLM_PROTOCOL=openai
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://REPLACE_ME/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=REPLACE_ME
# LLM_MODEL=REPLACE_ME
